WEBVTT

00:00.440 --> 00:03.720
Deploy gravity manipulation.

00:00.560 --> 00:03.730
<b>Deploy</b>

00:01.730 --> 00:03.730
<b>gravity
manipulation</b>

00:07.910 --> 00:10.010
Hypersonic countermeasures!

00:10.010 --> 00:11.890
But I didn't hear gunfire.

00:14.320 --> 00:16.560
You've fucked up, Detective Agency!

00:18.710 --> 00:21.700
I'm here to save your asses, 
on the boss's orders.

00:23.700 --> 00:26.300
Here we go. Time for a gunfight!

00:26.300 --> 00:27.950
Gravity manipulation!

00:35.590 --> 00:36.600
Grab on!

00:41.290 --> 00:42.470
Impossible...

00:43.010 --> 00:45.670
Is he a Detective Agency accomplice?

02:19.690 --> 02:22.690
To think we'd be saved by the Port Mafia...

02:22.690 --> 02:23.760
Saved?

02:23.760 --> 02:24.870
Idiot.

02:25.180 --> 02:27.860
Your boss made a deal with my boss.

02:28.340 --> 02:31.990
The price for your rescue is a transfer 
of one Agency member to the Mafia.

02:32.610 --> 02:36.140
We've always got room for Gifted 
criminals with useful abilities.

02:36.140 --> 02:37.080
The president did?

02:37.460 --> 02:39.330
No... well...

02:39.330 --> 02:43.620
We would all have been arrested, 
and Yosano-san would have been killed.

02:43.620 --> 02:44.940
You're right.

02:45.310 --> 02:48.020
Ideals alone can't save lives.

02:48.630 --> 02:50.190
We have to be practical.

02:51.180 --> 02:53.410
Do you think he hit his head or something?

02:53.410 --> 02:55.500
Maybe it's because his 
core got chopped up.

02:55.500 --> 02:56.690
His core?

02:56.690 --> 02:58.520
Oh, you mean his notebook.

02:59.270 --> 03:01.860
You have an interesting pulse, 
idealist Kunikida-san.

03:02.210 --> 03:05.700
You're relieved right now, aren't you?

03:06.670 --> 03:08.170
<i>Is he right?</i>

03:08.170 --> 03:10.560
<i>If my colleagues die, 
my ideals die with them.</i>

03:11.200 --> 03:13.190
<i>Am I waiting for that day?</i>

03:19.890 --> 03:20.830
Get back here.

03:25.540 --> 03:27.940
Dude, are you serious?

03:30.130 --> 03:30.930
Shit!

03:30.930 --> 03:33.450
That bastard's going to slash up the rotors!

03:35.640 --> 03:36.700
Tanizaki.

03:39.870 --> 03:41.980
Expose the actual murderer! And don't fail!

03:42.530 --> 03:44.200
Evil, begone.

03:45.460 --> 03:46.490
Please.

03:47.000 --> 03:48.200
Plum Blossoms in the Snow!

03:52.990 --> 03:54.220
Fool.

03:54.220 --> 03:56.330
I won't die falling from this height.

03:56.330 --> 03:58.860
I'll extend my sword again 
and chase the chopper.

03:58.860 --> 04:00.630
You're the fool here.

04:00.920 --> 04:03.410
I won't allow anyone to mess up my schedule!

04:03.720 --> 04:07.530
Your ideals are as lofty and 
large as a hot-air balloon,

04:07.530 --> 04:11.940
but a hot-air balloon inevitably runs 
out of fuel and returns to the ground.

04:11.940 --> 04:14.030
My name is Kunikida Doppo.

04:14.030 --> 04:15.810
My ideals will not fail.

04:15.810 --> 04:19.590
I will fuel them with my life so 
they will fly on for eternity!

04:16.880 --> 04:17.770
<b><i>Hand
 Grenade</i></b>

04:29.630 --> 04:31.540
Kunikida-san!

04:31.540 --> 04:34.540
<b>Episode 45
You, A Child of Sin;
 I, A Child of Sin</b>

04:35.080 --> 04:38.040
<b>Two days later</b>

04:54.160 --> 04:56.130
Kyouka-chan, are you okay?

04:57.220 --> 04:58.640
I'm a little tired.

04:59.080 --> 05:00.520
Of course you are.

05:00.520 --> 05:03.160
We've been sitting here for
 two days without drinking.

05:03.680 --> 05:06.130
I'm going to go look for food and water.

05:06.130 --> 05:07.710
I wonder if it's true...

05:07.710 --> 05:10.990
I heard the inspectors speaking.

05:11.430 --> 05:13.660
They said the president was arrested

05:13.660 --> 05:16.620
and Kunikida-san blew 
himself up during his escape.

05:16.620 --> 05:18.120
He may not have survived.

05:20.470 --> 05:22.340
How did it come to this?

05:24.230 --> 05:27.470
Survival is our priority right now.

05:28.050 --> 05:32.260
<b>no Akiko</b>

05:28.050 --> 05:32.260
<b>Fukuzawa Yukichi</b>

05:28.050 --> 05:32.260
<b>Kuniki</b>

05:28.060 --> 05:30.240
<i>What a terrible incident.</i>

05:30.240 --> 05:34.410
<i>A government-sanctioned detective agency 
turning out to be a terrorist organization...</i>

05:34.410 --> 05:40.470
<i>It's unbelievable, but there is video 
evidence of the crime and many witnesses.</i>

05:40.870 --> 05:46.410
<i>It's likely that the crimes they've solved in 
the past were in fact their own doing.</i>

05:47.730 --> 05:49.460
Hide your face.

05:49.460 --> 05:51.590
First, we need to secure 
funds to make our escape.

05:52.030 --> 05:54.110
Then we'll escape by train.

05:54.110 --> 05:56.800
Escape... And then?

05:57.430 --> 05:58.610
I don't know.

05:58.990 --> 06:00.450
The Decay of Angels...

06:00.450 --> 06:03.710
the ones behind all this... have 
an impeccable, far-reaching plan.

06:04.120 --> 06:08.670
We don't even have a full picture of 
their plot, let alone any evidence.

06:09.030 --> 06:10.760
<i>She's right.</i>

06:10.760 --> 06:13.540
<i>If this was really the 
Decay of Angels' doing,</i>

06:13.540 --> 06:15.880
<i>then Fyodor must be involved.</i>

06:16.560 --> 06:20.110
<i>There's no way the two of us could 
take down that monster alone.</i>

06:21.490 --> 06:23.800
The tiger is strong, 
but you're weak.

06:24.800 --> 06:27.790
<i>The Agency has saved me time after time,</i>

06:28.740 --> 06:31.690
<i>but I can't help the Agency.</i>

06:31.690 --> 06:33.920
You're giving up already?

06:40.230 --> 06:41.480
Is something wrong?

06:46.420 --> 06:47.210
<i>Right.</i>

06:47.920 --> 06:51.370
<i>What would Dazai-san do in this situation?</i>

06:53.280 --> 06:54.080
<i>There is...</i>

06:54.560 --> 06:58.140
<i>There's just one lead proving 
the Agency's innocence.</i>

06:58.420 --> 07:00.910
<i>The Detective Agency is about
 to get a huge job offer!</i>

07:00.910 --> 07:02.380
<i>Don't accept it!</i>

07:03.010 --> 07:04.700
Oguri Mushitaro?

07:04.700 --> 07:05.790
Yeah.

07:05.790 --> 07:08.750
He gave Rampo-san a warning 
just before the incident.

07:08.750 --> 07:11.280
He knew about the plan.

07:11.280 --> 07:14.000
He must know who the
 true murderers are, too.

07:14.000 --> 07:17.120
Maybe even how to restore the 
Detective Agency to the way it was.

07:17.570 --> 07:20.440
He's missing right now, though.

07:20.440 --> 07:22.200
How do we find him?

07:22.200 --> 07:23.660
There's always a way.

07:25.720 --> 07:26.810
Hello?

07:28.530 --> 07:30.960
Francis' Eyes of God?

07:33.420 --> 07:34.750
Is this safe, though?

07:34.750 --> 07:36.630
He was our enemy before.

07:36.630 --> 07:39.130
He might sell us out to the Military Police.

07:39.130 --> 07:41.350
He's agreed to hear us out.

07:44.810 --> 07:48.310
Dazai-san was able to get him to 
cooperate during the cannibalism.

07:49.050 --> 07:51.110
We'll have to try to do the same.

07:58.530 --> 08:00.280
I smell blood.

08:04.820 --> 08:06.190
Are you all right?

08:06.690 --> 08:08.510
It's you...

08:08.780 --> 08:10.530
I'm all right.

08:10.530 --> 08:11.460
So, hurry...

08:11.810 --> 08:13.460
Help Francis.

08:13.460 --> 08:14.970
Take care of her.

08:21.180 --> 08:24.820
You seem to have lost your religion 
quite spectacularly, priest.

08:25.180 --> 08:29.690
Death to my target, 
for my beloved princess...

08:29.690 --> 08:31.900
You mean Margaret.

08:31.900 --> 08:35.140
How touching that you 
would try to rescue her,

08:35.140 --> 08:36.800
even as you've lost everything.

08:36.800 --> 08:40.570
But you see, the disrespect 
of forgetting my face...

08:40.850 --> 08:42.170
is punishable by death!

08:42.630 --> 08:45.360
Physical boost: 50,000 dollars!

09:03.060 --> 09:04.350
He got away.

09:05.970 --> 09:07.460
<i>He's strong.</i>

09:07.460 --> 09:09.660
<i>I see why he was the 
leader of The Guild.</i>

09:10.170 --> 09:13.690
<i>But why was an assassin here now?</i>

09:19.920 --> 09:24.520
How is life in the Port Mafia hideout?

09:24.790 --> 09:29.080
It ought to conceal you from the
 Hunting Dogs for at least a week.

09:29.080 --> 09:30.250
Mori-sensei...

09:30.550 --> 09:33.960
Do you know if Kunikida 
survived the explosion?

09:33.960 --> 09:38.420
Unfortunately, all I was able to find 
out was where Dazai-kun has gone.

09:40.490 --> 09:45.460
Dazai-kun was already arrested by the 
Hunting Dogs prior to the hostage situation.

09:45.460 --> 09:47.900
Thee Military Police transferred
 him to the Ministry of Justice,

09:47.900 --> 09:49.100
then to Public Security.

09:49.440 --> 09:52.860
His subsequent whereabouts are unknown.

09:57.000 --> 09:58.950
The Detective Agency is innocent, you say?

09:59.260 --> 10:00.490
I swear.

10:00.490 --> 10:04.290
What about the footage on TV of the
 hostages being murdered, then?

10:04.290 --> 10:05.930
We were framed.

10:05.930 --> 10:07.750
The Decay of Angels are the masterminds.

10:08.250 --> 10:10.610
Fyodor is a co-conspirator.

10:20.810 --> 10:24.620
Even if, hypothetically, 
you speak the truth...

10:24.620 --> 10:26.760
The Detective Agency is doomed.

10:26.760 --> 10:29.440
Defeating Fyodor is impossible.

10:30.840 --> 10:37.070
He's currently held in a European 
detention center called Mersault.

10:37.940 --> 10:40.870
Mersault's very existence 
is a national secret.

10:40.870 --> 10:44.280
Its location is known only by high-level 
European government officials.

10:44.830 --> 10:46.760
Needless to say, access is impossible.

10:46.760 --> 10:49.750
In fact, it's the safest 
hideout in the world.

10:50.480 --> 10:51.460
Now...

10:51.850 --> 10:56.030
It would be a little annoying if the 
Agency were to use the Eyes of God.

10:56.030 --> 10:59.120
I ought to eliminate its owner,
 just in case.

11:01.180 --> 11:05.100
But if he's imprisoned, he shouldn't be able 
to give orders to the outside, either.

11:05.100 --> 11:08.090
That kind of thing is his specialty.

11:09.860 --> 11:13.770
In other words, it's impossible to beat him.

11:14.090 --> 11:18.750
It's like a game of chess where 
only he can move the pieces.

11:19.050 --> 11:20.260
There's nothing we can do.

11:22.880 --> 11:24.070
Spell Bullet!

11:25.990 --> 11:29.200
<i>He must have left his blood behind 
when the fountain pen hit it.</i>

11:29.470 --> 11:31.880
<i>I won't be able to boost 
my strength in time.</i>

11:31.880 --> 11:33.210
<i>I'm dead.</i>

11:40.640 --> 11:43.720
And now the Eyes of God is useless.

11:43.720 --> 11:46.940
I've devised a perfect plan.

11:47.780 --> 11:50.320
But perfection is boring, isn't it?

11:55.610 --> 11:57.440
A new prisoner?

12:04.070 --> 12:08.200
I activated the sprinkler 
system to dilute the blood.

12:08.200 --> 12:09.670
Kyouka-chan.

12:09.670 --> 12:11.150
You did this?

12:11.650 --> 12:14.620
But how did you know about the blood?

12:14.620 --> 12:18.340
I was under the stairwell when a 
warning showed up on the display.

12:19.550 --> 12:23.430
I've stopped your assassination attempt,
 mister demon.

12:25.680 --> 12:27.690
Well played.

12:28.030 --> 12:31.430
You let yourself be captured 
in order to save the Agency.

12:31.430 --> 12:36.050
The only way I can see through your 
schemes is by sitting here with you.

12:36.360 --> 12:40.020
I'm blessed to have a chess 
partner in a place like this.

12:44.500 --> 12:48.250
Chief Taneda is expected to 
awaken in the next 40 hours.

12:48.600 --> 12:51.790
If the procedure is successful, that is.

12:51.790 --> 12:53.110
Damn it...

12:53.110 --> 12:55.700
Why did the chief go after 
the enemy on his own?

12:56.180 --> 12:59.420
This wouldn't have happened 
if he'd had us protecting him.

12:59.420 --> 13:02.610
That was the criminal's condition.

13:02.610 --> 13:04.620
That we would meet each other alone.

13:04.620 --> 13:07.170
How could we fall for that?!

13:07.170 --> 13:08.640
It was for the information.

13:09.010 --> 13:14.530
The chief's Gift allows him to learn the
 details of any abilities activated nearby.

13:14.530 --> 13:19.600
He was confident, having previously 
 stopped violent Gifted using his ability.

13:19.910 --> 13:20.880
Alas...

13:21.960 --> 13:24.360
The criminal was one step ahead.

13:26.790 --> 13:28.680
Please watch over the chief.

13:28.680 --> 13:30.250
I'll give directions on-site.

13:30.250 --> 13:33.140
Wouldn't it be best if you 
stay until he awakens?

13:33.140 --> 13:34.350
No...

13:34.350 --> 13:37.240
I was never on very good 
terms with the chief.

13:38.080 --> 13:40.700
The chief quantifies human lives.

13:41.520 --> 13:44.640
Sacrifice one to save a hundred.

13:46.060 --> 13:47.990
I couldn't stand that.

13:49.360 --> 13:52.430
If you discover the
 Decay of Angels, kill them.

13:52.430 --> 13:54.770
But what of legal justice?

13:54.770 --> 13:55.760
Ango...

13:56.030 --> 13:57.980
What is the mission of the 
Special Operations Division?

13:58.830 --> 14:00.200
Peace.

14:00.200 --> 14:05.180
It is to bless the masses with an
 ignorant, peaceful existence.

14:05.180 --> 14:08.420
To hell with the law when 
peace is on the line.

14:08.700 --> 14:13.460
I will let even good men die for it.

14:14.120 --> 14:16.350
I was oblivious.

14:17.060 --> 14:20.970
When the chief said he'd have good 
men die for the sake of peace,

14:20.970 --> 14:23.630
he meant even himself.

14:24.490 --> 14:27.970
I'll report on the case's closure 
when the chief awakens.

14:28.580 --> 14:32.260
I will kill the murderer myself.

14:32.770 --> 14:36.670
Time for happy group life counseling!

14:36.670 --> 14:40.250
I, Fyodor, will be your host.

14:39.390 --> 14:41.740
Okay, stop right there! Hold up!

14:42.150 --> 14:43.320
Yes?

14:43.710 --> 14:44.820
Yes, what?

14:44.820 --> 14:46.250
Yes, what what?

14:47.880 --> 14:49.490
Counseling...

14:49.490 --> 14:51.940
Thank you for your
 prompt understanding.

14:51.940 --> 14:56.640
Our high intelligence allows us
 to read each other's minds.

14:56.640 --> 15:01.450
But, because of that, we aren't able 
to provide counseling to others.

15:01.760 --> 15:05.460
Unless they have our level 
of intelligence, that is.

15:05.460 --> 15:09.800
Which is why I'd like to take this opportunity
 to discuss our troubles with one another.

15:10.190 --> 15:11.820
Sure, then. You go first.

15:12.240 --> 15:13.170
All right.

15:13.460 --> 15:17.230
My subordinates are always waiting for 
my instructions. They lack initiative.

15:17.230 --> 15:20.900
How might I get them to become 
more autonomous and effective?

15:20.900 --> 15:23.880
Just sit around all day.

15:23.880 --> 15:27.770
Some of them will realize things have to change 
and take it upon themselves to act.

15:27.770 --> 15:29.650
I see.

15:29.650 --> 15:31.420
Okay, my turn.

15:31.420 --> 15:32.370
Go ahead.

15:32.370 --> 15:36.630
The waitress at the cafe won't 
respond to my advances.

15:36.630 --> 15:38.570
What should I do?

15:38.820 --> 15:42.870
Make her lose her job and trick 
her family into disowning her.

15:42.870 --> 15:45.290
That ought to convince her to turn to you.

15:45.890 --> 15:47.170
I see.

15:47.170 --> 15:51.130
<b>lololololol</b>

15:47.170 --> 15:51.130
<b>lololololol</b>

15:51.700 --> 15:54.540
Let's both ask a question at the same time.

15:54.540 --> 15:55.670
Sure thing.

15:56.090 --> 16:00.810
Tell me how you contact the outside world.

16:01.350 --> 16:03.200
I figured as much.

16:03.200 --> 16:04.480
Of course.

16:04.480 --> 16:07.290
Whichever of us learns the other's 
method of communication first

16:07.630 --> 16:11.810
will be able to ask our associates to 
terminate the other's ability to communicate.

16:11.810 --> 16:12.980
In other words...

16:13.420 --> 16:14.710
Victory.

16:15.040 --> 16:17.790
You won't see through my 
method of communication.

16:18.150 --> 16:19.790
Of course I will.

16:20.110 --> 16:21.720
That's why I'm here.

16:22.870 --> 16:24.490
Indeed...

16:24.490 --> 16:30.720
So the evidence you'd need to prove your 
innocence lies with this mushy taro man.

16:30.720 --> 16:32.610
It's Mushitaro.

16:32.610 --> 16:36.430
The vehicle transporting 
him was found on the road.

16:36.820 --> 16:39.930
All that was found was an 
officer who was shot dead.

16:39.930 --> 16:41.720
Mushitaro-san's blood was not there.

16:42.190 --> 16:44.680
The enemy must have abducted him.

16:44.680 --> 16:48.010
And you need the Eyes of God to find him.

16:50.240 --> 16:51.570
I wouldn't mind.

16:51.570 --> 16:53.370
Though, it would come at a price, of course.

16:53.370 --> 16:54.810
What's your price?

16:54.810 --> 16:58.130
You see, I'd like to 
bring Margaret back.

16:58.130 --> 16:59.440
Margaret...

16:59.870 --> 17:01.360
Your employee?

17:01.360 --> 17:04.080
She's currently in a coma.

17:04.080 --> 17:07.180
Have the Agency's doctor woman revive her.

17:07.590 --> 17:08.880
Yosano-san?

17:09.160 --> 17:13.130
Margaret is the one person 
who can kill Nathaniel.

17:14.230 --> 17:16.580
You saw the attack earlier.

17:16.890 --> 17:19.670
Nathaniel has become the Rats' pawn,

17:19.670 --> 17:22.210
but he still remembers her.

17:22.210 --> 17:27.950
His desire to save her has compelled 
him to commit incomprehensible acts.

17:27.950 --> 17:29.680
We'll take advantage of that.

17:29.680 --> 17:32.710
But wasn't it because she risked her life

17:32.710 --> 17:35.520
to protect Nathaniel that 
she was critically wounded?

17:36.200 --> 17:37.250
Correct.

17:37.480 --> 17:41.450
You're going to make two people, who tried
 to save each other, kill each other?

17:41.740 --> 17:42.940
What's wrong with that?

17:43.280 --> 17:44.580
I'd forgotten...

17:44.980 --> 17:47.580
You're the man who tried 
to crash the Moby Dick

17:47.580 --> 17:50.010
into the city and take hundreds 
of thousands of lives.

17:50.330 --> 17:51.500
Again, your point?

17:51.850 --> 17:54.050
I may have chosen the wrong 
person to do business with.

17:55.950 --> 17:56.960
Are you sure?

17:57.230 --> 18:01.010
I feel like the president would 
admonish me for making such a deal.

18:01.010 --> 18:02.580
Have our negotiations failed?

18:02.960 --> 18:04.010
Very well.

18:04.010 --> 18:07.450
But there's something I want 
to show you before you leave.

18:12.340 --> 18:13.910
Allow me to introduce her.

18:13.910 --> 18:15.400
This is Margaret.

18:19.960 --> 18:21.280
No...

18:22.300 --> 18:23.330
This is awful.

18:23.840 --> 18:25.980
During the Guild's bankruptcy,

18:25.980 --> 18:30.670
she was seen by several abhorrent doctors 
and her symptoms worsened.

18:31.240 --> 18:35.150
She only agreed to take on 
the Guild's dangerous duties

18:35.150 --> 18:37.570
to have resources to rebuild her family.

18:38.140 --> 18:40.980
At this point, that's a vain dream.

18:41.790 --> 18:45.040
If she could speak now,

18:45.040 --> 18:47.620
she would ask for her life support 
to be terminated immediately,

18:47.620 --> 18:51.560
and the money being used for her treatment
sent to her motherland instead.

19:02.710 --> 19:04.010
All right.

19:04.010 --> 19:05.310
I'll take your deal.

19:08.980 --> 19:10.790
Are you really sure about this?

19:11.190 --> 19:12.360
I'm hopeless.

19:12.960 --> 19:14.820
Whenever I see someone suffering,

19:15.800 --> 19:18.210
I see my younger self.

19:20.490 --> 19:22.010
I can't leave them.

19:36.700 --> 19:38.900
I think that's a philosophy
 that works well for you.

19:39.980 --> 19:40.900
Let's go.

19:42.470 --> 19:45.460
<i>I hope Yosano-san and the others are safe.</i>

19:45.460 --> 19:47.150
Don't give me that bullshit.

19:47.150 --> 19:51.150
You can't help us prove 
the Agency's innocence?

19:51.150 --> 19:52.220
That is correct.

19:52.220 --> 19:54.300
The agreement with Fukuzawa-dono

19:54.300 --> 19:56.690
was that we would only help the Agency

19:56.690 --> 20:00.430
in exchange for transferring one 
of its members to the Mafia.

20:00.430 --> 20:02.860
Transfer a member of the Agency?

20:02.860 --> 20:04.280
Do you think you're funny?

20:04.280 --> 20:07.920
All you really want is for me 
to join the Mafia, don't you?

20:09.060 --> 20:11.540
That's right. What of it?

20:11.540 --> 20:14.560
Fukuzawa-dono understood that when 
he made the agreement with me.

20:14.830 --> 20:16.980
The president would never agree to that.

20:19.270 --> 20:23.190
I accept your request in regards to 
protecting the Detective Agency employees.

20:23.710 --> 20:27.200
Though combating the Hunting Dogs 
will be quite the daring endeavor,

20:27.200 --> 20:29.290
even for the Port Mafia.

20:29.290 --> 20:30.840
<i>What are your demands?</i>

20:30.840 --> 20:35.170
The transfer of an Agency 
member to the Port Mafia.

20:35.170 --> 20:38.110
<i>That's not an easy price to pay.</i>

20:39.350 --> 20:40.880
<i>I have one condition.</i>

20:41.220 --> 20:42.850
You don't request Yosano-kun.

20:43.230 --> 20:47.420
She would never be able to tolerate 
being your assistant again.

20:48.970 --> 20:50.270
You're wrong.

20:50.590 --> 20:54.070
Fukuzawa-dono said he would 
be willing to give you up.

20:58.970 --> 21:02.290
Boss, pardon the interruption.

21:02.560 --> 21:05.010
This radio was at the entrance.

21:05.010 --> 21:07.570
<i>Hey, how're you doing, old sport?</i>

21:07.940 --> 21:10.550
<i>I don't have time. I'll make it quick.</i>

21:10.550 --> 21:13.180
<i>I sent the lycanthrope boy your way.</i>

21:13.180 --> 21:14.360
Lycanthrope...

21:14.770 --> 21:16.210
Atsushi-kun!

21:16.210 --> 21:17.570
He's alive!

21:17.570 --> 21:19.220
What's the reason for his appearance?

21:19.220 --> 21:20.630
A transaction.

21:20.630 --> 21:23.100
Use the healing ability for me.

21:23.100 --> 21:26.680
In exchange, I'll provide information that
 will lead to the Agency's restoration.

21:26.970 --> 21:28.650
<i>We'll meet in twenty minutes.</i>

21:28.650 --> 21:29.860
<i>At Goban Street.</i>

21:30.660 --> 21:33.140
Information that'll lead to 
the Agency's restoration!

21:33.140 --> 21:34.570
Now we have some hope.

21:34.570 --> 21:35.900
Odd.

21:36.370 --> 21:39.400
How did he discover this hideout?

21:39.840 --> 21:42.860
He must have used his 
Eyes of God or whatever, right?

21:42.860 --> 21:44.020
That's the thing.

21:44.280 --> 21:46.650
If he was able to discover this hideout,

21:46.650 --> 21:49.770
he might as well have done business 
with the Military Police instead.

21:50.130 --> 21:53.720
It would have been more profitable to 
do the formidable Hunting Dogs a favor,

21:53.720 --> 21:55.740
as opposed to the weakened Detective Agency.

21:56.080 --> 22:01.610
The Francis I know always sides with 
the stronger, more bullish side.

22:03.300 --> 22:07.210
This transaction may be a trap.

23:37.890 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode: 46

23:37.890 --> 23:40.010
<i>A Dream of Butterflies</i>
